WEBVTT

00:01.980 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:03.460 --> 00:07.080
Satoshi challenged the Eisetsu Gym for his eighth badge.

00:08.040 --> 00:10.170
However, he suffered a crushing defeat at the hands of Gym Leader Urup.

00:11.120 --> 00:13.960
It was his second time in a row getting knocked out, the first being against Shota.

00:15.520 --> 00:16.480
And on that night,

00:17.240 --> 00:20.600
Satoshi disapppeared in a forest alone...

00:37.630 --> 00:38.810
Now even Gekkouga is...

00:39.230 --> 00:39.600
Yes.

00:40.570 --> 00:43.720
It has recovered its stamina so I don't think there's any need to worry, but...

00:44.150 --> 00:45.270
...do you know where it went?

00:47.640 --> 00:49.060
I wonder where it's gone.

00:49.900 --> 00:51.750
It probably followed Satoshi.

01:14.630 --> 01:15.670
The Winding Woods... The Dawn of Evolution!

01:22.820 --> 01:23.380
I...

01:24.490 --> 01:25.030
I've got to...

01:25.790 --> 01:26.950
I've got to get my act together...

01:29.000 --> 01:29.770
I...

01:36.550 --> 01:38.690
Satoshi will come back, right?

01:37.980 --> 01:47.830
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:37.980 --> 01:47.830
Z

01:39.190 --> 01:40.090
Do not worry.

02:11.900 --> 02:13.480
Hey, where's Serena?

02:23.000 --> 02:24.420
What's he doing?

02:24.420 --> 02:25.590
He's looking at the sky.

02:25.830 --> 02:26.880
Why the sky?

02:27.120 --> 02:28.410
I don't know.

02:28.410 --> 02:30.410
If the brat boy is alone, that means...

02:31.510 --> 02:32.560
...this is our chance...

02:32.980 --> 02:34.010
...to get Pikachu.

02:52.840 --> 02:53.530
Satoshi.

03:02.870 --> 03:03.390
Sorry...

03:04.310 --> 03:05.500
...for leaving so suddenly.

03:06.560 --> 03:09.860
Satoshi, if there's something troubling you,

03:10.290 --> 03:12.420
talk to me about it! It can be anything.

03:14.960 --> 03:17.460
If I can be of any use to you, no matter how little...

03:21.700 --> 03:23.960
I know how you feel, Satoshi.

03:24.800 --> 03:27.430
Back when I failed at my Tripokalon,

03:28.320 --> 03:28.890
I wondered why I...

03:29.400 --> 03:31.140
What do you know about it, Serena?!

03:37.000 --> 03:38.100
Why don't you talk, then?!

03:38.540 --> 03:39.700
This is my problem.

03:40.090 --> 03:40.980
Just leave me be!

03:48.610 --> 03:50.110
The Satoshi I know...

03:50.700 --> 03:52.790
...is always full of energy and a leader and...

03:53.670 --> 03:54.560
...works hard and...

03:55.160 --> 03:55.810
...is optimistic and...

03:56.750 --> 03:58.650
...never gives up till the end!

03:59.350 --> 04:00.240
So I...

04:00.560 --> 04:01.190
I...

04:04.160 --> 04:05.170
Right now,

04:05.980 --> 04:07.190
you're not yourself at all.

04:15.390 --> 04:16.560
Not myself...

04:17.190 --> 04:17.590
...huh...?

04:27.340 --> 04:29.000
Oh, geez!

04:37.910 --> 04:39.190
I'm done! I'm done!

04:39.500 --> 04:40.540
I'm done with this after all!

04:40.990 --> 04:42.390
Just brooding over it the whole time...

04:42.760 --> 04:44.260
That's just not me!

04:45.670 --> 04:46.870
When you don't know what to do, move!

04:47.580 --> 04:49.430
Moving will help you make some kind of realization.

05:05.600 --> 05:06.580
Ow...

05:07.390 --> 05:07.570
Hm?

05:17.090 --> 05:18.290
That was close.

05:33.600 --> 05:36.470
Now Serena's gone off somewhere too! How boring!

05:36.870 --> 05:38.550
I am sure she will be back soon.

05:39.780 --> 05:41.100
Speaking of the devil...

05:45.230 --> 05:47.210
Serena, where have you b...

05:49.100 --> 05:50.110
I don't care any more!

05:53.440 --> 05:54.910
I wonder if something happened.

06:01.200 --> 06:01.800
It's snowing!

06:02.950 --> 06:04.180
Everyone, get in!

06:04.940 --> 06:06.830
I heard the snowfall is going to become heavier later.

06:07.350 --> 06:08.240
Okay.

06:11.110 --> 06:11.910
I don't care!

06:15.810 --> 06:18.320
Aw, geez! I get it already!

06:21.590 --> 06:23.040
Serena, what's wrong?

06:23.830 --> 06:27.050
I have to bring Satoshi back here before the weather gets rough, even if it means I have to use force.

06:27.420 --> 06:27.940
It's dangerous out there, after all!

06:28.390 --> 06:28.990
I'm coming too!

06:31.200 --> 06:33.380
Ah, wait! Our backpacks!

06:39.430 --> 06:41.290
I'm sorry about today, Gekkouga.

06:42.410 --> 06:44.360
If I had got my act together...

06:45.270 --> 06:47.560
...we should've been able to draw out that power of yours.

06:48.840 --> 06:50.100
If only I had got my act together...

07:06.970 --> 07:08.120
It's safe here.

07:09.110 --> 07:10.490
This is bad...

07:20.550 --> 07:21.630
Satoshi!

07:21.990 --> 07:23.210
Satoshi!

07:23.460 --> 07:24.630
Answer!

07:27.340 --> 07:29.090
This is where he <i>was</i>, but...

07:36.390 --> 07:37.900
Have you found him, Rentorar?

07:42.260 --> 07:43.090
Satoshi!

07:43.600 --> 07:44.900
I can't see a thing!

07:48.410 --> 07:48.860
Ha!

07:51.350 --> 07:53.900
Pika-chan, where are you going all by yourself?

07:53.900 --> 07:56.470
How convenient that you got separated from the brat boy.

07:56.470 --> 07:57.960
Let's get Pikachu!

08:00.790 --> 08:02.470
Oh no, you won't!

08:08.920 --> 08:09.750
Did you two feel it too?

08:10.160 --> 08:11.170
It's kinda...

08:11.170 --> 08:12.940
...unremarkable, or how should I put it...

08:13.270 --> 08:15.200
Like, it doesn't travel down to the tail bone or anything.

08:16.950 --> 08:18.620
Fire one more.

08:24.530 --> 08:24.950
Huh?

08:24.950 --> 08:25.290
Huh?

08:25.290 --> 08:27.270
Hey, take us seriously!

08:28.290 --> 08:30.360
Your electric shocks are kinda weak!

08:38.710 --> 08:40.610
This feels bad!

08:41.490 --> 08:42.380
...Or not.

08:44.210 --> 08:45.950
Where's the edge you usually have?

08:47.240 --> 08:48.850
Why have you become so weak?

08:48.850 --> 08:50.600
Is it because the brat boy's not here?

08:51.270 --> 08:54.940
What now? Getting a weak Pikachu would be...

08:54.940 --> 08:57.870
You're right. There's no point if it doesn't have its usual power.

08:59.410 --> 09:00.100
Let's go, let's go.

09:00.360 --> 09:01.600
Yeah, let's go home.

09:04.830 --> 09:05.680
Pikachu!

09:07.840 --> 09:08.910
Has something happened?

09:12.640 --> 09:14.980
We need to find Satoshi quickly or he will be in danger.

09:16.960 --> 09:17.750
Satoshi...

09:23.020 --> 09:23.950
Pokémon Quiz.

09:24.300 --> 09:25.130
The answer is...?

09:27.060 --> 09:36.930
Coming up next:

09:27.060 --> 09:32.030
Satoshi and Gekkouga get caught up in a storm

09:27.980 --> 09:32.700
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

09:32.060 --> 09:36.930
What answers will they come to...?

09:44.570 --> 09:45.530
Bro...!

09:45.940 --> 09:46.910
Are you all right, Eureka?

09:47.610 --> 09:48.550
I feel like I'm gonna get blown away.

10:00.940 --> 10:01.490
Squishy!

10:10.710 --> 10:11.940
Bro, look!

10:12.490 --> 10:13.910
Squishy found this for us!

10:14.230 --> 10:15.790
For the time being, let us take a break there.

10:16.110 --> 10:16.550
Yeah.

10:20.830 --> 10:21.480
Satoshi...

10:22.210 --> 10:23.470
I hope he's safe.

10:24.150 --> 10:25.670
He's fine, Serena.

10:26.820 --> 10:31.020
Earlier, I just lost my cool and said something horrible to Satoshi.

10:31.990 --> 10:32.520
But that's because...

10:33.470 --> 10:36.390
To me, Satoshi is someone I admire...

10:37.510 --> 10:38.320
I get it.

10:39.020 --> 10:39.910
I feel the same way.

10:41.970 --> 10:44.840
Let us search for Satoshi as soon as the blizzard has passed.

10:45.730 --> 10:45.990
Yeah.

10:55.310 --> 10:56.710
Why don't you join me instead of staying out there?

10:59.750 --> 11:00.520
It's fine.

11:07.140 --> 11:08.850
Come on, it's fine.

11:18.070 --> 11:20.070
Let's all stay together until it stops.

11:21.410 --> 11:21.830
All right, come on.

11:22.520 --> 11:23.110
Come in, come in.

11:24.470 --> 11:24.840
See?

11:25.340 --> 11:26.800
If we stay like this we'll be warm.

11:56.390 --> 11:57.610
Ah, those Kofuurai are...!

11:58.430 --> 11:59.980
Everyone, stay here.

12:28.600 --> 12:30.030
All right, just one more.

12:30.870 --> 12:31.830
Hold on.

12:40.800 --> 12:41.620
All right, grab my hand.

12:44.070 --> 12:44.510
Come on.

12:45.030 --> 12:45.560
Do your best.

12:46.140 --> 12:46.860
Work up your courage!

12:52.710 --> 12:53.670
Hold on to me.

12:54.030 --> 12:54.830
Let's join the others.

12:59.110 --> 13:00.240
All right, good kid.

13:14.520 --> 13:15.220
Gekkouga!

13:17.600 --> 13:18.210
Oh no!

13:24.440 --> 13:25.110
I want to save it...

13:32.900 --> 13:34.740
We can do this!

13:45.720 --> 13:46.820
Go!

13:56.670 --> 13:57.690
It's a branch! Dodge it!

13:58.120 --> 13:58.460
To the right!

14:01.100 --> 14:02.310
Another one! Dodge!

14:08.190 --> 14:09.260
Decrease your speed.

14:09.660 --> 14:10.090
There!

14:17.950 --> 14:19.190
All right!

14:22.790 --> 14:24.820
Everything's fine now, Kofuurai.

14:30.290 --> 14:30.920
Gekkouga...

14:32.420 --> 14:33.180
Thank you.

14:36.260 --> 14:37.340
I've worried you, huh?

14:37.620 --> 14:38.200
I'm sorry.

14:45.750 --> 14:48.270
You know, something like this has happened before.

14:49.930 --> 14:51.010
When I was little,

14:51.730 --> 14:57.260
I wanted to meet some Pokémon, so I went off into the woods alone, but I ended up getting lost.

15:00.850 --> 15:03.990
Then I took shelter from the rain together with some Pokémon, just like now.

15:05.750 --> 15:07.580
I was so happy at that moment...

15:08.520 --> 15:12.420
I couldn't wait to become a Trainer and go on adventures together with Pokémon.

15:14.700 --> 15:15.910
I'm sorry, Gekkouga.

15:16.710 --> 15:19.190
I promised we'd become strong together, after all.

15:20.250 --> 15:21.500
Being alone made me realize something.

15:22.210 --> 15:26.940
After making my promise to Shota, I wanted my badge so badly and was so desperate to win against Urup-san.

15:27.510 --> 15:28.700
I somehow got impatient.

15:29.570 --> 15:33.130
I thought that, since I'm the Trainer, I need to work harder. That I need to pull myself together.

15:33.800 --> 15:36.950
But that's not doing one's best <i>together</i>.

15:37.910 --> 15:39.390
When I look beside me, I see a friend.

15:40.310 --> 15:41.530
A friend I love a lot.

15:42.310 --> 15:46.920
Earlier, I wanted to save Kofuurai together with you, no matter what.

15:47.630 --> 15:49.800
Because you were with me, we were able to do it.

15:55.070 --> 15:57.190
Gekkouga, please lend me your power.

15:57.990 --> 16:00.080
Let's start over from zero.

16:01.950 --> 16:02.650
Let's go together.

16:11.980 --> 16:13.750
Everything's all right now, guys.

16:45.330 --> 16:46.690
The blizzard has stopped.

16:47.350 --> 16:49.010
I wonder if Satoshi is all right...

16:55.960 --> 16:56.540
Huh?

17:04.150 --> 17:04.910
Guys.

17:09.060 --> 17:09.630
Pikachu!

17:10.170 --> 17:11.830
I'm sorry for worrying you.

17:12.390 --> 17:14.520
Geez! We've been looking for you!

17:14.750 --> 17:16.000
What is most important is that you are safe.

17:16.390 --> 17:17.730
Everyone, I'm sorry.

17:20.060 --> 17:20.710
Satoshi...

17:21.340 --> 17:22.460
Thank you, Serena.

17:23.920 --> 17:25.700
Serena, your words were my wake-up call.

17:28.780 --> 17:30.440
Welcome back, Satoshi!

17:34.440 --> 17:35.310
Can you hear us?

17:35.990 --> 17:37.350
Satoshi and Gekkouga...

17:37.850 --> 17:40.030
Even when apart, they thought of one another,

17:40.430 --> 17:42.820
and worked together to attain a new bond.

17:43.680 --> 17:44.560
We think...

17:44.950 --> 17:49.530
...it is fine to have faith in this world full of Pokémon and humans.

18:02.710 --> 18:03.940
Yo, everyone!

18:04.770 --> 18:05.630
Rocket Gang!

18:06.080 --> 18:08.200
We were waiting for you to come back.

18:08.540 --> 18:10.920
Pikachu, now we'll try to get you once more!

18:10.920 --> 18:12.040
Exactly!

18:16.430 --> 18:18.670
Yeah! It really is different from before.

18:19.000 --> 18:20.360
Its expression has changed.

18:20.970 --> 18:22.530
Pumpjin, Dark Pulse!

18:23.090 --> 18:23.950
Maaiika!

18:24.370 --> 18:25.410
Psybeam!

18:29.140 --> 18:30.870
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

18:39.990 --> 18:41.680
It's effective, it's effective! This one's effective!

18:42.020 --> 18:43.380
That's right! This is it!

18:43.840 --> 18:45.010
This is the power we meant!

18:47.190 --> 18:48.780
What a good Thunderbolt it was!

18:49.320 --> 18:52.300
In the end, it has to be <i>that</i> Pikachu and no other.

18:52.600 --> 18:53.450
You're right!

18:54.270 --> 18:55.740
Let's revise our plans again!

18:57.610 --> 19:00.200
It feels good that this feels bad!

19:06.280 --> 19:08.930
Look, everyone! Miare City's on TV.

19:10.030 --> 19:11.710
You are right! I wonder what this is about.

19:12.230 --> 19:16.620
It has been decided that the Kalos League will be held in Miare City this time!

19:17.060 --> 19:19.380
Oh? So the League will be in Miare City, huh?

19:19.940 --> 19:21.970
Preparations are advancing steadily.

19:22.440 --> 19:25.390
There's no doubt this tournament will be lively as well!

19:27.180 --> 19:28.430
Yeah, I know.

19:29.070 --> 19:30.270
Today is the day we'll seal the deal!

19:30.840 --> 19:31.900
Let's go, Gekkouga!

19:33.430 --> 19:34.000
Uh?

19:34.510 --> 19:35.400
Hm? What's the matter?

20:03.350 --> 20:04.800
I understand, Gekkouga.

20:05.600 --> 20:06.980
I won't stand still any more.

20:07.510 --> 20:08.800
We'll make straight for the League.

20:09.590 --> 20:10.120
Let's go...

20:10.580 --> 20:11.470
...to the Eisetsu Gym!

20:17.900 --> 20:18.860
All right, the next episode...

20:19.430 --> 20:20.970
...will take place in the Eisetsu Gym again!

20:28.780 --> 20:30.910
Pokémon Unbelievable!

20:32.430 --> 20:36.520
This is Pokémon Unbelievable, which features the mysterious ecology of Pokémon!

20:36.860 --> 20:38.750
Take this Gekkouga, for example.

20:39.150 --> 20:45.000
It sometimes undergoes a phenomenon that not only drastically increases its physical capabilities, but also changes its appearance to resemble its Trainer.

20:46.210 --> 20:50.720
According to legend, a Pokémon like this existed in a certain village in the Kalos region.

20:51.030 --> 20:56.510
Well, that's what the legend says, but research on the matter hasn't advanced at all, so there are still many mysteries to it.

20:58.000 --> 21:01.550
Really though, Satoshi and Satoshi Gekkouga really are similar!

21:01.800 --> 21:03.280
I'm kinda jealous!

21:04.050 --> 21:05.210
You are right, they are similar.

21:05.210 --> 21:08.000
I wonder if Dedenne can turn into Eureka Dedenne too.

21:10.600 --> 21:12.820
Eureka Dedenne, Nuzzle!

21:15.330 --> 21:17.530
It is powerful!

21:17.700 --> 21:19.630
A chill just went down my spine for some reason...

21:20.960 --> 21:25.930
Sunday May 29th at 8am!

21:21.500 --> 21:24.040
Pokémon Fan
Louis Kurihara

21:22.160 --> 21:24.820
Louis Kurihara's appearance throws the place into a complete chaos!

21:28.320 --> 21:30.210
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.350 --> 21:31.510
Towards our next adventure!

21:32.590 --> 21:33.750
I won't feel at a loss any more.

21:34.480 --> 21:36.580
The friends I love are right here.

21:37.190 --> 21:38.480
I realize that now,

21:38.850 --> 21:39.290
so I'll never again...

21:40.910 --> 21:44.260
Come on, try to melt my ice with your fiery passion!

21:45.210 --> 21:47.740
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:48.200 --> 21:53.140
Satoshi Gekkouga VS Mega Yukinooh! The Giant Water Shuriken Triggers!!

21:52.470 --> 21:55.940
Next Time

21:52.470 --> 21:55.940
Satoshi Gekkouga VS Mega Yukinooh!
The Giant Water Shuriken Triggers!!

21:53.600 --> 21:55.460
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:55.980 --> 22:05.950
Next episode:

21:55.980 --> 22:00.920
The Eisetsu Gym rematch!

21:56.960 --> 22:01.540
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

22:01.000 --> 22:05.950
Will they get the badge this time!?
